## Project Overview
This project features the 3D parametric design and motion assembly of a classic Reciprocating Steam Engine powertrain. The assembly models a complete slider-crank mechanism designed to convert linear fluid pressure (thermal steam expanding inside a cylinder) into continuous rotational mechanical energy. 

The assembly highlights advanced kinematic configuration, part-to-part bearing fits, rotational inertia distribution, and standardized mechanical interfaces built completely within SolidWorks.

